 ## Desktop formal audio foundation
 
 - `DesktopVoiceAudioStore` persists immutable MP3 artifacts under the selected root `audio/generated`, with independent ownership/hash receipts, bounded streams and atomic publication. It has no startup orphan sweep; corrupt indexes, missing receipts and unknown files remain preserved. Formal clips use a separate 16 MiB / 30-minute structural/native profile; picker preview stays at its accepted 16 MiB / 120 seconds. Both profiles use the same Windows backend with explicit per-port duration admission.
-- `DesktopVoicePlayback` provides key-independent ordered playback and stop/join. `DesktopAudioFocus` provides separate formal/preview ports over one MCI output; a superseded port cannot stop the current owner. AppContainer owns formal voice drain before preview/native output and root release.
+- `DesktopVoicePlayback` provides key-independent ordered playback and stop/join. `DesktopAudioFocus` provides separate formal/preview ports over one MCI output; a superseded port cannot stop the current owner. AppContainer owns formal voice drain before preview/native output and root release. Queue admission checks the originating UI foreground token inside the playback mutex; leaving and returning cannot revive a delayed click. Replacement releases a queued/active old voice through native stop before deleting its artifact.
 - `DesktopFishGenerationCoordinator` adapts official targets, text confirmation, global five-permit batches, history/replacement and foreground autoplay. `DesktopFishVoiceTransport` reuses shared TTS serialization with one-shot/one-exchange transport and callback/body drain. Only explicit `s2.1-pro-free` is authorized; stale/paid models fail, and the dated free profile fails closed after 2026-11-30 pending re-verification. Artifact cleanup re-reads a complete strict reference inventory; uncertain commits preserve audio. Exact durable voice readback may confirm a post-write exception before refreshing the repository. `DesktopFishTtsAdmission` shares five permits across formal and picker TTS, through actual body drain.
 
 - `DesktopChatVoiceRuntime` and `DesktopChatVoicePanel` wire explicit assistant segment/whole generation, bound narrator choice, auxiliary-cost confirmation, new take vs replacement, version-scoped voice bars, ordered playback, stop, export and explicit delete. Primary chat mutations drain voice jobs before editing/deleting/switching versions; foreground leases drop autoplay on screen/session leave. No assistant completion automatically requests TTS. Formal playback holds a data-operation lease through native stop/close. Existing message/image mutations retain their own normal/exclusive scopes; do not wrap image cleanup in an outer normal lease. The lazy owned auxiliary text transport drains its real sockets/executor at app shutdown.
